{:builder-laws
 ["Root nodes MUST set explicit full-canvas w/h (an unstyled root defaults to 160x160 and clips almost anything)."
  "The harness root also sets pad-all 0 AND border-width 0: the stock card style's PAD_DEF=24 on the root would clip full-bleed cells (tabview large 460x320, scale vertical-large 56x360, table large 480x240) and skew x/y probes, and the asgard panel border (1px/edge) shrinks the root content box to canvas-2 so an exactly-canvas-wide cell reads clipped with root scroll extent. Root pad/border-zeroing is harness geometry, never theme styling of the widget under test."
  "Buttons need an explicit child WIDGET_LABEL (the renderer builds an empty lv_button; text is a separate child)."
  "State is applied ONLY via the wire node.states bitmask (:states-bits), except where a state is a widget-prop bit by contract (switch/checkbox :checked ride their props messages; those cards carry the residual bits only)."
  "Fresh renderer context per card (hash comparisons)."
  "Widget slugs derive from the WidgetType enum."]
